{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261108T195417Z-13204b4c", "ts": "2026-11-08T19:57:31Z", "actor": {"worktree": "arrt", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "feature/observed-taste", "build": "39144ab1f1d5"}, "body": {"base_commit": "8b2932afe8bf6d9a91307ee43f9ed143b4b51dd1", "base_tree": "c38bab2f9e7bad94ff82006e02343c1eb5ae4028", "head_tree": "8f4375b1988948224da1095a5729a4f8f683ce6a", "head_commit": "87cc502e50b72d0782048e82c69b1da8f74ae16c", "dispatch_commit": "87cc502e50b72d0782048e82c69b1da8f74ae16c", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/taste.js", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/dedup.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/discovery_records.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/sqlite_discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_taste_and_reactions.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_observed_taste.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/information-architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md", "arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/taste.js", "arrt/src/arrt/library/discovery/dedup.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/discovery_records.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/sqlite_discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py", "arrt/tests/browser/test_taste_and_reactions.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_observed_taste.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/information-architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "blocking", "title": "record-lint chunk-ref-missing: Chunk 01's deliverable `library/services/taste.py` does not resolve", "recommendation": "Relayed from the manifest's record_lint (chunk 01, line 58): the declared deliverable `library/services/taste.py` does not exist at that path. The code exists at `arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py`, so this is a paperwork defect: write the deliverable as a repo-relative path the deliverable check resolves (and do the same for any other bare package path in Chunks 01 and 02). Scope: instance.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "record-lint unchecked: the graded chunk was inferred as Chunk 01", "recommendation": "record_lint graded chunk 01 because the dispatch named no chunk, so it has said nothing about Chunk 02's deliverables (the cumulative-final chunk this review closes). Passing the chunks to critic-begin would let the check grade both. Scope: none.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "An observed row is frozen beside a stated one under another spelling, and the two contradict each other", "recommendation": "`observe_artist` returns as soon as any `stated` row shares the artist_key, before it looks at the `observed` rows. When the observed row comes first and the stated one arrives later under a different value, both rows stay. Example: review writes observed `likes` for \"Salvador Dali\", then the curator clicks *Not this* on the artist page for \"Salvador Dal\u00ed\". `set_affinity` upserts on (kind, value), so it adds a second row, and from then on the observed row is never updated or withdrawn, at a verdict or at `reobserve`. Taste, Ask and phase 1 then carry a stated `declines` next to an observed `likes` whose counts never change. That is the contradiction `set_affinity`'s docstring says the unique index exists to prevent. The fix: when a stated row under the key exists, delete the observed rows under that key (the stated row outranks them, so nothing is lost). Add a test that writes the observed row first and then states under another spelling, which `test_a_stated_judgment_under_another_spelling_is_never_overwritten` does not cover because it states first. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py", "arrt/tests/unit/test_observed_taste.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No test checks that an existing observed row's counts are refreshed", "recommendation": "No test makes a further verdict on an artist who already has an observed row and checks that the stored rationale's counts change. The case is 5 of 5 rejected, then a 6th, which should read 'Rejected 6 of the 6 ...'. `test_a_falling_share...` goes through None and writes a new row. The stated test returns early. The inferred test changes derivation, so the equality short-circuit is never tested on rationale alone. If the rationale were dropped from the equality tuple at taste.py:212-217, or the observed-to-observed update were skipped, the Taste screen and prompts would show stale counts, and the change fragment promises those counts. Add one example through `set_verdict` that asserts the rationale after the 6th verdict and that the row's id is unchanged. Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/tests/unit/test_observed_taste.py", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "A test's name says the inferred row is replaced, but its assertions show it is kept", "recommendation": "`test_an_inferred_judgment_is_replaced_by_what_the_verdicts_show` seeds an inferred row under a different key (\"Klimt, Gustav\") and asserts that it stays beside a new observed row. So it actually tests that a different key is left alone. The replacement is tested by `test_an_inferred_judgment_of_the_same_artist_is_corrected_in_place`. Rename it (for example, `..._under_another_key_is_left_alone`) so its name matches its assertions (core.md: 'When you drop or rewrite a test's assertion, ... re-read the test's name against it'). Scope: instance.", "files": ["arrt/tests/unit/test_observed_taste.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Forgetting an observed judgment on Taste is undone by the next verdict or the next startup, while the dialog promises nothing brings it back", "recommendation": "Instance. Before this change every row the Forget dialog deleted stayed deleted. `observe_artist` now re-creates an observed row from the verdicts on any accept or reject of that artist, and `Services.reconcile` -> `TasteService.reobserve` re-creates it at every startup even when nothing new was decided. The curator who clicks 'Forget it' on an observed row reads in the dialog (`screens/taste.js` `forget`) that 'nothing brings the judgment back', and the row is back after the next restart. No persisted state records that the curator dismissed it. Choose one of two fixes and test it through the route. (a) Make forget stick: record the dismissal by `artist_key` and have `observe_artist` honour it until the verdicts change. (b) Keep the current behaviour and make the dialog depend on the derivation: for an observed row, say it returns while the verdicts hold, and point to correcting it, which writes a stated row that review never overwrites. With (b), the consumer note's 'only lasts until the next decision on that artist' should also mention startup. That note is an oracle record, so it is flagged here for the builder and not rated.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/http/static/screens/taste.js", "arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "observe_artist enforces derivation precedence under artist_key on some branches only, so persisted rows can diverge from the verdicts", "recommendation": "Class: the precedence (stated, then observed, then inferred, per artist_key) has no single model, and each branch of `observe_artist` handles a different subset. Two reachable sequences show the gap. (1) An observed 'declines Dali' exists, and the curator then states 'loves Dal\u00ed' through Ask or Taste. `set_affinity` matches on the exact value, so it inserts a new row. From then on `observe_artist` returns early on the stated row and never updates or withdraws the observed one. Taste and every prompt's `describe_taste` carry both rows with frozen counts, which contradicts the docstring's 'the row always reflects the verdicts as they stand'. (2) An inferred row is converted in place to observed (tested in `test_an_inferred_judgment_of_the_same_artist_is_corrected_in_place`). If the share later falls below 90%, the withdrawal branch deletes that row, and the inferred judgment and its rationale are gone for good, although no caller can write `inferred` any more. That contradicts the module docstring's 'The `inferred` rows already in the catalogue stay'. Fix: when a stated row exists under the key, withdraw any observed rows under it before returning. For inferred rows, either keep them (write the observed row beside them, or convert back on withdrawal) or record the deletion as intended and correct the module docstring. Add one test per sequence: observed first, then stated under another spelling, then more verdicts; and inferred, then observed, then a falling share.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "Plan Goals still carry six 'Inferred' rulings, and one shipped behaviour (deleting an observed row does not last) is recorded nowhere but the consumer note", "recommendation": "Instance. build-plan-observed-taste.md \u00a7 Goals keeps an 'Inferred (the boundary review shows these)' list that this cumulative review is the boundary for: (1) an artist is its artist_key, written under the latest verdict's name, and a stated row under any spelling with that key blocks; (2) observed replaces an inferred row; (3) unattributed works count for nobody; (4) wanted/pending count for neither side; (5) startup re-derives every artist in Services.reconcile; (6) the rationale carries the counts. None is the owner's ruling yet, and they ship as product behaviour. Separately, a seventh decision the code makes with no recorded why: observe_artist keeps no tombstone, so a curator's delete of an observed row is undone by the next verdict on that artist or by the next start (TasteService.reobserve). That is a real product choice (a delete is not a refusal; only a correction to a stated row is durable), and it appears only in .prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md's consumer note, not in data-model.md \u00a7 Affinity or the plan. Put the seven to the owner in one question, then record the answers (or the inferred status cleared) in the plan and the deletion rule in data-model.md beside the observed-writer paragraph.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/taste.py", "arrt/src/arrt/services/container.py"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner", "recommendation": "Scope none. Decisions made in building, and what settled each: the thresholds and mirror rule (owner, 2026-11-08, agents-and-memory.md open question 1); the observed write runs inside set_verdict's transaction so a verdict and its taste commit together (builder; consequence: a failure in observe_artist now fails the curator's verdict rather than only the taste); the artist read is a dedup-key prefix via substr, not LIKE, so no key character acts as a wildcard (builder); the share compared as a Fraction so 9 of 10 is exactly 90% (builder); startup re-derivation also visits artists that only have an observed row, so a row whose verdicts vanished is withdrawn (builder); an existing row is corrected in place under its current name rather than renamed, because the unique index is on the name (builder). Alignment: the plan's Chunk 02 deliverable naming api-contract.md's art_taste refusal text needed no edit, since that text already carried the 2026-11-08 Direction note.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/library/services/discovery.py", "arrt/src/arrt/persistence/sqlite_discovery.py"], "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "Consumer note says deleting an observed judgment lasts until the next decision on that artist; the next start re-creates it too", "recommendation": "Records Pass, bar 'it ships'. Instance. .prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md \u00a7 Consumer note: 'Deleting one only lasts until the next decision on that artist.' Services.reconcile now calls TasteService.reobserve at every start, which calls observe_artist for every artist with decided works and inserts the row afresh while the rule holds. So a curator who deletes an observed row and makes no further decision on that artist still sees it return after a restart, and reads the product as ignoring the delete. Change the sentence to 'until the next decision on that artist or the next start of Arrt' (or remove the claim). The correction-to-stated remedy the note gives is true: set_affinity writes only stated, and observe_artist returns early on a stated row under the same artist_key.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md"], "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: 'the review path that will one day assert observed' survives in a test docstring", "recommendation": "Instance; prose, nothing reads it. Rule: 'When you retire, amend, descope or close anything, first grep the whole repo (no --include) for its nouns and OLD wording'. The diff amended this exact sentence in validated_write's docstring (taste.py) but arrt/tests/unit/test_taste_service.py:89 still says the write path is a function 'precisely so the review path that will one day assert `observed` goes through the same checks'. Make it relational (name observe_artist) the next time that file is touched; no fix commit wanted for it alone. Learnings read: .claude/rules/learnings/core.md and .claude/rules/learnings/surface.md (from learnings-files --for-diff). The change conforms to surface's 'When a repair keeps a stored derived value current, trigger it on the stored value differing from a fresh derivation': observe_artist compares the fresh derivation against the stored row and reobserve runs at every start, so a rule change reaches every row.", "files": ["arrt/tests/unit/test_taste_service.py"], "fid": "R-11"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog Reconciliation: no open item affected or resolved", "recommendation": "Scope none. backlog cache-query --repo brookstalley/arrt affecting <the 14 changed files> returned 0 items (cache confirmed 2026-11-08T18:13Z). The open set has no item on taste, verdicts or affinities (the only near match on those words, #97, is about observed documents, unrelated). Nothing to mark shipped; C-B1 to C-B4 do not fire, since the diff adds and cites no backlog item.", "fid": "R-12"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 6, "note": 5}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": "observed-taste", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "8b2932afe8bf6d9a91307ee43f9ed143b4b51dd1", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/information-architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/observed-taste.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md", "findings": [{"check": "chunk-ref-missing", "path": "chunk 01", "line": 58, "detail": "declared deliverable `library/services/taste.py` file does not exist"}], "unchecked": ["chunk-ref-missing graded chunk 01 of .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-observed-taste.md: chunk 01 was inferred as the plan's first open chunk (`plan_status.current_chunks`) because the dispatch carried no chunk \u2014 a chunk whose review is not yet recorded is still open, so this may be the next chunk rather than the reviewed one"], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 1, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-08T19:54:19Z"}}

